Package: ofeIntegrateR
Title: Design, Sample and Analyse On-Farm Strip Experiments
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Zhanglong", "Cao", , "zhanglong.cao@curtin.edu.au", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A workflow for on-farm experimentation (OFE) strip trials,
    from planning a trial to estimating its treatment effects. Lays out strip
    and stacked designs with randomised or systematic treatment order; works
    out how many point samples a target precision needs and where to put them;
    aggregates irregular yield-monitor data onto an estimable lattice; derives
    pseudo-environments from the spatial covariance of the dense layer; and
    fits spatial mixed models by residual maximum likelihood with separable
    'ASReml'-style residual structures -- 'ar1()', 'exp()', 'diag()' and
    'dsum()' sections -- written in base R, so that the analysis needs no
    commercial licence. Sparse point-source variables (soil cores, tissue
    tests) can be integrated with the dense layer by a kriged covariate or a
    joint bivariate spatial model. 'ASReml-R' is used automatically where it
    is licensed. Developed for the AAGI-CU-RD-OFE GRDC project.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
